# A complaint, answered (IDEAS I20 d, I20 e, I23, I25 c; QUESTIONS Q29, 6; board 0.7). It came up from collab/scenarios/wanted.
# Story: as Arbor comes, no ring is drawn round the window in front, nothing stands in for a window that moves, the menu bar has one icon,
# and the wallpaper behind docked windows is as it was.
open Safari
open Notes
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
focus 101
expect ring none
get focusRing
expect replied false
get menuBarControls
expect replied false
# Nothing to change: it is 0 as Arbor comes. (`get` would not tell 0 from 0.46 by the word 0.)
set animationDuration 0
expect replied is already 0
# Nor is the wallpaper darkened behind the two, or a line drawn round the Desktop between them.
scene
expect replied backdrop: none
set dimBehindArranged 0
expect replied is already 0
set desktopEdge 0
expect replied is already 0
# One icon whatever happens: with a window framed, a view saved, the view held, Arbor paused.
menu-bar
expect replied a single icon
zoom 101
save-view 1
menu-bar
expect replied a single icon
expect ring none
hold
menu-bar
expect replied a single icon
release
pause
menu-bar
expect replied a single icon
resume
show-all
# Each is an option still, one line away, and one line takes it back.
set focusRing true
expect ring 101
set menuBarControls true
menu-bar
expect replied forward
set dimBehindArranged 0.25
scene
expect replied backdrop: dim 0.25
reset dimBehindArranged
reset focusRing
reset menuBarControls
expect ring none
menu-bar
expect replied a single icon
